<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Net pay from a payslip</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>PAYE tax bands for resident individuals, from 1 July 2023 (Kenya Revenue Authority; Finance Act 2023):</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Monthly taxable pay (Ksh)</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Rate</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">First \(24\,000\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(10\%\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Next \(8333\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(25\%\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Next \(467\,667\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(30\%\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Next \(300\,000\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(32.5\%\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Above \(800\,000\)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(35\%\)</td></tr></table><p>Personal relief: Ksh \(2400\) a month, taken off the tax. PAYE is never negative.</p><p>{@nm@}'s payslip for one month shows:</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Payslip, {@nm@}</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Ksh</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Basic pay</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@ksh(B)@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Allowances</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@ksh(Al)@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Pension contribution (taken off before tax)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@ksh(pen)@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">Other deductions, in total (after tax)</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@ksh(oth)@}\)</td></tr></table><p>(a) Find the taxable pay.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the PAYE.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Find the net pay.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p><p>Give each answer to the nearest shilling, or exactly in cents.</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Gross pay \(= {@ksh(B)@} + {@ksh(Al)@} = {@ksh(G)@}\). Taxable pay \(= {@ksh(G)@} - {@ksh(pen)@} = {@ksh(tp)@}\).</p><p>Split Ksh \({@ksh(tp)@}\) into the bands:</p><ul><li>first \({@ksh(min(tp,24000))@}\) at \(10\%\): \({@ksh(min(tp,24000)/10)@}\)</li>[[if test="is(tp>24000)"]]<li>next \({@ksh(min(tp,32333)-24000)@}\) at \(25\%\): \({@ksh((min(tp,32333)-24000)/4)@}\)</li>[[/if]][[if test="is(tp>32333)"]]<li>next \({@ksh(min(tp,500000)-32333)@}\) at \(30\%\): \({@ksh((min(tp,500000)-32333)*3/10)@}\)</li>[[/if]]</ul><p>Tax before relief \(= {@ksh(taxf(tp))@}\).</p><p>(b) PAYE \(= {@ksh(nr)@} - 2400 = {@ksh(py)@}\).</p><p>(c) Net pay \(=\) gross pay \(-\) pension \(-\) PAYE \(-\) other deductions \(= {@ksh(G)@} - {@ksh(pen)@} - {@ksh(py)@} - {@ksh(oth)@} = {@ksh(net)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
